The way you can write code of the target DSL without wrapping it in a string both gives me fears and excitement:<p><pre><code>    solver.assert((&amp;x + 4).eq(7));
</code></pre>
My subconsciousness shouts <i>&quot;MISSING QUOTES&quot;</i> while my ratio says <i>&quot;Calm down, that&#x27;s nice and clean and safe and how it&#x27;s supposed to be - ever has been&quot;</i>.
